{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואיש את קדשיו לו יהיו", :translit "ve'ish et kedashav lo yihyu", :gloss "and a man's consecrated things shall be his"} {:he "פרשת סוטה", :translit "parshat sotah", :gloss "the passage of the sotah"} {:he "קיני הנשים", :translit "kinei ha-nashim", :gloss "the women's jewelry"} {:he "בני עלי", :translit "benei eli", :gloss "the sons of Eli"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut): the topic of withheld offerings placed adjacent to sotah to infer wrongdoing."}], :frame {:text "The sons of Eli took from the offering pot by force before the fat was burned, violating the sacred portions; for this sin their lineage was cut off (1 Samuel 2:12-17, 2:30-36). The passage of the suspected adulteress follows immediately after the verse about consecrated things (Numbers 5:10–5:12), so Ba'al HaTurim reads the adjacency as a warning that withholding what is owed to God is tantamount to the sotah's betrayal.", :sources ["1 Samuel 2:12-17" "1 Samuel 2:30-36" "Numbers 5:10" "Numbers 5:11-12"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Juxtaposition (semikhut): the topic of withheld offerings placed adjacent to sotah to infer wrongdoing.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:26:57.380958290Z", :model "glm-5.2"}